  "note": "calculateCOPM() averages up to 5 answered performance scores and 5 answered satisfaction scores (1-10 each) independently, defaulting each average to 0 when nothing is answered. Both category labels are computed by the SAME copmPerformanceCategory() helper, so satisfactionCategoryLabel reads 'Good performance' rather than 'Good satisfaction' even for a satisfaction score - a naming quirk in the shared label function, not a bug in the score itself. detectAdditionalFlags() does independent free-text substring matching (case-insensitive) on several narrative fields (cognition, homeEnvironment, socialSupport, pain, lowerExtremity, coordination, vision, fatigue), so persona narrative text was chosen deliberately to trigger, or deliberately avoid, those substrings.",
